{"name":"Calico Dress","hex":"#3d4e67","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calico","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of rough cloth made from unbleached and not fully processed cotton, often printed with a bright pattern.","Ellipsis of calico cat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of calico or resembling the color of calico cloth, having a pattern of red and contrasting areas; variegated.","Having red, brunette, and blond hair colors, resembling the fur of a calico cat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calico"},{"term":"dress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put clothes (or, formerly, armour) on (oneself or someone, a doll, a mannequin, etc.); to clothe. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To put clothes (or, formerly, armour) on (oneself or someone, a doll, a mannequin, etc.); to clothe. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An item of clothing (usually worn by a woman or young girl) which both covers the upper part of the body and includes a skirt below the waist.","An item of clothing (usually worn by a woman or young girl) which both covers the upper part of the body and includes a skirt below the waist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calico","blocks":[{"text":"Calico is a heavy plain-woven textile made from unbleached, and often not fully processed, cotton. It may also contain unseparated husk parts. The fabric is coarser than muslin, but less coarse and thick than canvas or denim. It is still very cheap owing to its unfinished and undyed appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Calico_Sample.JPG/330px-Calico_Sample.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico","wikidata":"Q1132695"},{"title":"Dress","blocks":[{"text":"A dress is a one-piece outer garment that is worn on the torso, hanging down over the legs. Dresses often consist of a bodice attached to a skirt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg/330px-Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dress","wikidata":"Q200539"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg/330px-Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg/330px-Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sample of calico printed with a six-colour machine by Walter Crum & Co., from Frederick Crace Calvert, Dyeing and Calico Printing (1878)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg/500px-Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg/1280px-Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg/500px-Calico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Calico printing (1835)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalico_printing_Wellcome_L0011294.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Dress_MET_19.181.1_F2.jpeg/500px-Dress_MET_19.181.1_F2.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th